{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Rename `_anthropic_cache_settings` to `_anthropic_cache_options`\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`_anthropic_cache_settings` in `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py` returns a pydantic-ai\n`ModelSettings` mapping (or `None` for a non-Anthropic model), not a settings object. Readers\nhave twice mistaken it for a config accessor. Renaming it to `_anthropic_cache_options` makes the\nreturn shape read correctly at every call site. Pure rename: no behaviour change, no signature\nchange, no new capability.\n\n## Approach\n\nRename the definition, then update every reference — including the ones that name the symbol as\na string, which a rename refactor will not touch.\n\n## Scope\n\nI went through the tree with `grep` and these are the files that mention it:\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py` — the definition (line 39) and the module docstring (line 10).\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — the re-export import (line 28) and the call site (line 337).\n- `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` — the import (line 17) and four direct call sites\n  (lines 313, 317, 318, 319).\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py` — line 90, where the symbol is named\n  as a **string literal** inside `monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, \"_anthropic_cache_settings\", …)`.\n  A rename refactor will not touch this; after the rename the patch would silently target a name\n  that no longer exists.\n- `docs/code-navigation.md` — four occurrences, where this symbol is the worked example.\n- `docs/serena-symbol-reference-coaching-sample.md` — two occurrences, same reason.\n\n## Testing\n\nEvery acceptance criterion is checked by a command that runs in-session and produces observable\noutput:\n\n- `git grep -n _anthropic_cache_settings` must print nothing and exit 1.\n- `git grep -n _anthropic_cache_options` must print the definition, the re-export, the call site,\n  the test call sites, the monkeypatch string, and the doc occurrences.\n- `make test` must pass, exercising the renamed function through `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`\n  and the monkeypatch through `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git grep -n _anthropic_cache_settings` prints nothing and exits 1 (the old name is gone\n      from the whole tree, including docs and the string literal)\n- [ ] `_anthropic_cache_options` is defined in `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py`, re-exported from\n      `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, called at the cache-settings site, and used at all four\n      `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` call sites, verified by `git grep -n _anthropic_cache_options`\n- [ ] `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py:90` patches the NEW name, verified by\n      `git grep -n '\"_anthropic_cache_options\"' tests/`\n- [ ] behaviour is unchanged: the function still returns the cache-control settings mapping for an\n      `anthropic:` model and `None` for `openai:`/`google-gla:`/`\"\"`\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` all pass"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785387631674452001,"uuid":"448613f7-39a1-4523-a8b3-06f440d71e14"}